+## Subtopics
+
+### [Image Bounds Check](15846-image-bounds-check.md)
+Verifies whether 2D coordinates lie within normalized image plane boundaries (0 to 1). It serves as a guard clause in ray-image frame intersection logic to prevent out-of-bounds memory access or invalid sampling when projecting rays onto the image plane. Unlike sibling methods that compute intersection points, this method performs a simple validity test with epsilon tolerance to handle floating-point precision errors near the edges. Choose it when a fast validity check is needed instead of full intersection computation.
+
 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity**: $O(1)$ per ray per boundary. The computation involves a fixed number of arithmetic operations.
-*   **Memory Complexity**: $O(1)$ auxiliary space.
-*   **Performance**: Highly efficient for parallel execution on GPUs due to lack of branching and simple arithmetic [G].
-*   **Strengths**: Exact analytic solution; no iteration required; suitable for culling and boundary checks.
-*   **Limitations**: Only computes intersections with the image frame boundaries, not with arbitrary geometry. Requires valid camera intrinsics [S1, S2, unofficial].
